    [Feature][Model] Support DeepSeek V4.1 decoder bounded replay (#17496)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Add decoder bounded replay for DeepSeek V4.1 on Ascend MRV2, following
    vllm-project/vllm#58132.
    
    For eligible prefill requests, layers after the last KV-source layer
    process only the final sliding-window tokens. Earlier layers process the
    full batch. Decode tokens and rows required for prompt logprobs are
    preserved.
    
    - Prepare replay batches and independent attention metadata through the
    MRV2 model-state hook.
    - Coordinate replay decisions and token counts across DP ranks,
    including idle ranks.
    - Gather rows, positions, query boundaries, and slot mappings with a
    Triton kernel.
    - Handle sequence-parallel states and DSA CP indexer buffers, then
    scatter retained outputs and auxiliary hidden states back to their
    original positions.
    - Reuse upstream Ascend SWA visibility bounds and preserve encoder-side
    replay boundaries for prefix-cache hits.
    
    The implementation targets MRV2 only and adds no MRV1 runner changes.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Decoder replay is controlled by `swa_bounded_replay=True` in `LLM`,
    or `--swa-bounded-replay` in the CLI.
    
    Supported configurations require MRV2 and `NONE` or `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`.
    Trimming runs only in eager steps; graph steps retain the full batch.
    Prefix caching uses the existing encoder-side bounded replay support.
    
    Sequence parallelism requires DSA CP. Speculative decoding is limited to
    DSpark with a compatible sliding window. MRV1, PP, PCP, DCP,
    microbatching, LoRA, and configurations with Engram layers after the
    replay boundary disable decoder replay with a warning.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Waiting to be tested.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: Yizhou Liu <liu_yizhou@outlook.com>

